<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Cut</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Edit &gt; Cut</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + X</b></span></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Cut</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command deletes the visible selection and places it in the clipboard. You may cut whole entities as well as parts of them. Data in the clipboard is available for KUBE only. This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden.</span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Cut</span> <span lang="EN-GB">and</span> <span class="Command">Copy</span> <span lang="EN-GB">commands both place selected data in the clipboard. The difference between them is that</span> <span class="Command">Cut</span> <span lang="EN-GB">removes the selection from the document while</span> <span class="Command">Copy</span> <span lang="EN-GB">preserves it.</span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Cut</span> <span lang="EN-GB">acts in the same way as</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command" style="text-decoration:none;">Delete</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command with the exception that it keeps removed data in the clipboard. In combination with</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command" style="text-decoration:none;">Paste As New Entity</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">in the same document</span> <span class="Command">Cut</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is equivalent to</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command" style="text-decoration:none;">Create New Entity From Selection</span></u><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
